  "causes": [
    {
      "id": "c1spoxu",
      "headline": "the inner spacing of 2 of 4 `<div>` elements shrank by 12 to 16 px, on all 4 changed screenshots, 100% of changed pixels",
      "text": "## the inner spacing of 2 of 4 `<div>` elements shrank by 12 to 16 px, on all 4 changed screenshots, 100% of changed pixels (`.ui-col`, c1spoxu)\n- for example, the \"Col\" element's inner spacing shrank by 12 px, at `getByText('Col')` in \"s1 >> renders\" (s4udgzc)\n- `.ui-col` from `framework-*.css` (layer `framework.components`) now sets font-weight (was 400, now 700); changed its declaration of color (was #0000ff, now #ff0000); no longer sets padding-left (values differ per element: `npx whydiff explain c1spoxu`)\n- it moved from unlayered into layer `framework.components`: its declarations now lose to any declaration of the same property outside a layer, whatever the selectors' specificity\n- to restore it: change the rule in the source file that builds `framework-*.css`, or set the old values in your own stylesheet if the rule comes from a dependency; whydiff cannot tell from a built sheet which it is\n- all occurrences: `npx whydiff explain c1spoxu`",
      "key": "k2|rule|framework-*.css|.ui-col|",
      "kind": "rule",
      "level": 0,
      "summary": {
        "kind": "rule",
        "selector": ".ui-col",
        "sheet": "framework-*.css",
        "layer": "framework.components",
        "sets": [
          "font-weight"
        ],
        "changed": [
          "color"
        ],
        "unsets": [
          "padding-left"
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "prop": "color",
            "from": "rgb(0, 0, 255)",
            "to": "rgb(255, 0, 0)"
          },
          {
            "prop": "font-weight",
            "from": "400",
            "to": "700"
          }
        ],
        "layerTo": "framework.components"
      },
      "scope": "global",
      "match": "exact",
      "ambiguous": 0,
      "screenshots": 4,
      "elements": 4,
      "pixels": 9600,
